module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.QuotientRingSheafOpenSubspace
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GradedAlgebraDescentQuotientIso

/-!
# The ideal generated on an open subspace, and the descent along the identified quotient

Let `X` be a ringed space and `U` an open of it.
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.QuotientRingSheafOpenSubspace` identifies the
quotient of the structure sheaf of `X.restrict U`, formed there, with the open-subspace reading of
a quotient of the slice structure sheaf `O_X|_U` — provided the two sheaves of ideals have the same
sections. That hypothesis is the content, different ideals having different quotients, and this
file supplies it for the ideals the local statements of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] actually generate,
namely the sheaves of ideals generated by a morphism into the structure sheaf.

Such an ideal is `Stacks.Sites.idealOfHom`, a **local closure**: its sections over an object are
the sections lying in the objectwise image after restriction along some covering sieve. So the
identification is not the objectwise one; what it needs is that local closure commutes with the
slice/open-subspace site equivalence, and that in turn is a statement about *sieves*, proved here
once for an arbitrary functor of sites.

With the hypothesis supplied, the transport of
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.descend` along the identified quotient —
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.descendRingIsoHom` of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GradedAlgebraDescentQuotientIso` — is instantiated
at the open-subspace spelling, which is the second half of this file.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.functorPullback_mem_iff`: **the sieve lemma.** For a functor of sites which is
  cover-preserving and cocontinuous, a sieve on an image object covers exactly when its
  functor-pullback does. Both halves are one line, and together they are the whole reason a local
  closure may be read on either site.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_localClosure_openSubspace_iff`: **local closure commutes with the
  open-subspace site equivalence.** Two submodules of the underlying presheaves of the two unit
  objects with the same sections at corresponding objects have local closures with the same
  sections there.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_openSubspace`: **the hypothesis
  `openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` consumes, for the sheaves of ideals generated by a morphism.** If
  a morphism into the structure sheaf of `X.restrict U` and one into the slice structure sheaf
  have the same objectwise image at corresponding objects, the sheaves of ideals they generate
  have the same sections there. The hypothesis is objectwise and therefore checkable; the
  conclusion is about the local closures.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_openSubspaceEquiv`: the canonical case of the
  previous one, where the morphism downstairs is the pushforward of the morphism upstairs off the
  slice site. The objectwise hypothesis is then `Iff.rfl`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isExteriorAlgebra_descend_openSubspaceRingQuotient`: **the universal
  property of an exterior algebra crosses the identification of the two quotients.** A sheaf of
  graded algebras on `X.restrict U` annihilated by the kernel of the quotient formed there whose
  descent along that quotient is an exterior algebra has its descent along the open-subspace
  reading of the slice quotient an exterior algebra too, on the generator read through the
  transport. This is `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.isExteriorAlgebra_descend_of_ringIso` at the
  open-subspace spelling, with only one annihilation hypothesis: the comparison being an
  isomorphism, the two quotient maps have the same kernel.

## Implementation notes

**Two spellings, and the reconciliation is to route through one of them.** The source of
`Stacks.Sites.quotientRingHom` on the slice site is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (X.sheaf.over U)`, while
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingHom` reads its argument out of
`(structureSheafRing X).over U`.
These are one sheaf of rings — `rfl` identifies them — but the two terms are
`sheafCompose ∘ overPullback` and `overPullback ∘ sheafCompose` of the same sheaf of commutative
rings, in the two orders, and nothing short of unfolding both functors and using structure eta
reconciles them. Instance search does not do that, so the local-surjectivity instances the two
descents take are not found when the two spellings meet, even though each is found alone. The same
happens one level down: `(openSubspace U).sheaf` carries the site
`Opens.grothendieckTopology ↑↑(openSubspace U).toPresheafedSpace`, which is
`Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U` only after unfolding `Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspace`.

The fix is not to thread instance hypotheses. It is to name each sheaf of rings once, as a
**reducible** abbreviation whose ascribed type pins the spelling — `openSubspaceSheaf` for the
structure sheaf of the open subspace at the `↥U` spelling of its site, `sliceRingSheaf` for the
slice structure sheaf at the `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf` spelling — and to state every
instance at those. The one instance that cannot simply be cited at the new spelling,
local surjectivity of the pushforward of a locally surjective quotient map, is re-proved from
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_whisker`, which speaks only of the underlying
presheaf morphism and is therefore indifferent to how its source sheaf is written.

**The general local-surjectivity instance for a quotient map is declared here.** The library had
it only for `Stacks.Sites.idealOfHom`
(`Stacks.RegularSequence.isLocallySurjective_quotientRingHom_idealOfHom`), although its proof uses
nothing about the ideal; `Stacks.Sites.isLocallySurjective_quotientRingHom` below is the same
proof for an arbitrary sheaf of ideals, which is what the comparison of two quotients needs.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute.** Nothing here is a clause of Tag 0BQY, whose statement is about the
comparison `⋀ⁱ(Ext¹) ⟶ Extⁱ`; this is the second of the two transports its gluing step consumes.
The 0BQY caveats in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulSelfExtExteriorLocal`
record the state.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0942](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0942)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.Sites


/-- **A sieve on an image object covers exactly when its functor-pullback does**, for a functor of
sites which is cover-preserving and cocontinuous.

The two halves are the two hypotheses. Cover preservation pushes the pullback forward to a
covering sieve, and the pushforward of a pullback is contained in the original sieve, so the
original covers. Cocontinuity is the converse by definition. -/
theorem functorPullback_mem_iff {Cs : Type*} [Category Cs] {Ct : Type*} [Category Ct]
    (Js : GrothendieckTopology Cs) (Jt : GrothendieckTopology Ct) (F : Cs ⥤ Ct)
    (hF : CoverPreserving Js Jt F) [F.IsCocontinuous Js Jt]
    {V : Cs} (S : Sieve (F.obj V)) :
    Sieve.functorPullback F S ∈ Js V ↔ S ∈ Jt (F.obj V) := by
  refine ⟨fun h => Jt.superset_covering ?_ (hF.cover_preserve h), fun h => F.cover_lift Js Jt h⟩
  rintro T g ⟨W, w, v, hw, rfl⟩
  exact S.downward_closed hw v

section

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{u} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}} [HasWeakSheafify J CommRingCat.{u}]

/-- **The quotient map `O ⟶ O/I` is locally surjective, as a morphism of sheaves of rings.** This
is `Stacks.Sites.isLocallySurjective_toQuotientRingSheaf` read through the forgetful functor to
`RingCat`, whose components are the same functions and whose image sieves are therefore the same
sieves. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_quotientRingHom (I : IdealSubsheaf O) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (quotientRingHom I).hom where
  imageSieve_mem {_X} y :=
    haveI := isLocallySurjective_toQuotientRingSheaf I
    Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J (toQuotientRingSheaf I).hom y

end

end Stacks.Sites

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

open Stacks.Sites
open _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (U : Opens X.carrier)

/-- **The structure sheaf of the open subspace `U`, at the `↥U` spelling of its site.** The type
ascription is the point: `(openSubspace U).sheaf` carries the site
`Opens.grothendieckTopology ↑↑(openSubspace U).toPresheafedSpace`, which is the topology on `↥U`
only after unfolding `Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspace`, and instance search does not unfold
it. Being an abbreviation, this is transparent to instance search in the other direction. -/
abbrev openSubspaceSheaf : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) CommRingCat.{u} :=
  (openSubspace U).sheaf

/-- **The slice structure sheaf of rings `O_X|_U`, at the `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf`
spelling.** This is the source of `Stacks.Sites.quotientRingHom` on the slice site. It is the same
sheaf of rings as `(structureSheafRing X).over U`, the source of the argument of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingHom`, but the two terms compose `sheafCompose` with
`overPullback` in the two orders; naming this one and stating every instance at it is what makes
instance search succeed where the two meet. -/
abbrev sliceRingSheaf : Sheaf ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) RingCat.{u} :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (X.sheaf.over U)

/-- **The structure sheaf of rings of `X.restrict U`, at the
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf` spelling and the `↥U` spelling of its site.** This is the
source of `Stacks.Sites.quotientRingHom` for a sheaf of ideals formed on `X.restrict U`, and — by
the definition of the pushforward off the slice site — also the source of the open-subspace reading
of a quotient map of the slice structure sheaf. -/
abbrev openSubspaceRing : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) RingCat.{u} :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (openSubspaceSheaf U)

/-- The two spellings of the slice structure sheaf of rings are one sheaf of rings. -/
theorem sliceRingSheaf_eq : sliceRingSheaf U = (structureSheafRing X).over U := rfl

/-- The two spellings of the structure sheaf of rings of the open subspace are one sheaf of
rings: the pushforward of the slice structure sheaf off the slice site is, by definition, the
structure sheaf of `X.restrict U`. -/
theorem openSubspaceRingSheaf_sliceRingSheaf_eq :
    openSubspaceRingSheaf U (R' := sliceRingSheaf U) = openSubspaceRing U := rfl

/-- **The open-subspace reading of a morphism out of the slice structure sheaf of rings**: its
pushforward off the slice site, with source written as `openSubspaceRing U` rather than as the
pushforward of `sliceRingSheaf U`. -/
abbrev openSubspaceQuotientHom
    {R' : Sheaf ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) RingCat.{u}}
    (α : sliceRingSheaf U ⟶ R') :
    openSubspaceRing U ⟶ openSubspaceRingSheaf U (R' := R') :=
  (openSubspaceRingPushforward U).map α

/-- **The open-subspace reading of a locally surjective morphism out of the slice structure sheaf
of rings is locally surjective.** This is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_openSubspaceRingHom` at the source `sliceRingSheaf U`
rather than `(structureSheafRing X).over U`. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_openSubspaceQuotientHom
    {R' : Sheaf ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) RingCat.{u}}
    (α : sliceRingSheaf U ⟶ R')
    [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) α.hom] :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U)
      (openSubspaceQuotientHom U α).hom :=
  Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_whisker (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U)
    ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) (openSubspaceSiteFunctor U) α.hom

/-! ### Local closure across the site equivalence -/

/-- **Local closure commutes with the open-subspace site equivalence, on sections.** Let `N` be a
submodule of the underlying presheaf of the unit object of the slice structure sheaf and `N'` one
of the unit object of the structure sheaf of `X.restrict U`, with the same sections over
corresponding objects. Then their local closures have the same sections there.

Unfolding both memberships leaves the two sieves of a section, and they correspond: the
restriction maps of the structure sheaf of `X.restrict U` are those of the slice structure sheaf
at the image objects, so the sieve downstairs is the functor-pullback of the sieve upstairs. The
covering conditions then agree by `Stacks.Sites.functorPullback_mem_iff`, the site functor of the
open subspace being a dense subsite and so both cover-preserving and cocontinuous. -/
theorem mem_localClosure_openSubspace_iff
    (N : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val.Submodule)
    (N' : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (openSubspaceRing U)).val.Submodule)
    (hN : ∀ (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ)
        (s : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (openSubspaceRing U)).val.obj V),
      s ∈ N'.obj V ↔ s ∈ N.obj (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)))
    (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ)
    (s : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (openSubspaceRing U)).val.obj V) :
    s ∈ (localClosure _ N').obj V ↔
      s ∈ (localClosure _ N).obj (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) := by
  refine Iff.trans (mem_localClosure_obj N' V s) (Iff.trans ?_
    (mem_localClosure_obj N (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) s).symm)
  rw [show N'.toSubfunctor.sieveOfSection s =
      Sieve.functorPullback (openSubspaceSiteFunctor U)
        (N.toSubfunctor.sieveOfSection s) from by
    ext W g
    exact hN (op W) _]
  exact functorPullback_mem_iff _ _ _ (Functor.IsDenseSubsite.coverPreserving _ _ _) _

variable [HasWeakSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) CommRingCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) CommRingCat.{u}]

omit [HasWeakSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) CommRingCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) CommRingCat.{u}] in
/-- **The hypothesis `Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` consumes, for the sheaves
of ideals generated by a morphism into the structure sheaf.** Let `φ` be a morphism into the slice
structure sheaf and `φ'` one into the structure sheaf of `X.restrict U` with the same objectwise
image over corresponding objects. Then the sheaves of ideals they generate have the same sections
there.

The hypothesis is objectwise and so is checked by computing two images; the conclusion is about
`Stacks.Sites.idealOfHom`, which is a local closure, and crossing that is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_localClosure_openSubspace_iff`. -/
theorem sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_openSubspace
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (sliceRingSheaf U)}
    (φ : F ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U))
    {F' : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (openSubspaceRing U)}
    (φ' : F' ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (openSubspaceRing U))
    (hφ : ∀ (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ)
        (s : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (openSubspaceRing U)).val.obj V),
      (∃ m, φ'.val.app V m = s) ↔
        (∃ m, φ.val.app (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) m = s))
    (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ) :
    sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := openSubspaceSheaf U) φ') V =
      sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := X.sheaf.over U) φ)
        (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) :=
  SetLike.ext fun s =>
    mem_localClosure_openSubspace_iff U (presheafRangeSubmodule φ.val)
      (presheafRangeSubmodule φ'.val)
      (fun W t =>
        ((mem_presheafRangeSubmodule_obj φ'.val W t).trans ((hφ W t).trans
          (mem_presheafRangeSubmodule_obj φ.val _ t).symm)))
      V s

omit [HasWeakSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) CommRingCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) CommRingCat.{u}] in
/-- **The canonical case: a morphism pushed forward off the slice site generates the
open-subspace reading of the ideal it generates.** The forward functor of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceEquiv` is the pushforward along the site functor
(`openSubspaceEquiv_functor`), so the pushed-forward morphism is the original one read at the
image objects and the objectwise hypothesis of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_openSubspace` is `Iff.rfl`.

This is the form in which `Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` is fed when the
ideal downstairs is the one a slice-site morphism generates; a consumer whose morphism
downstairs is built on `X.restrict U` in its own right, as the local Koszul statements build
theirs, owes instead the objectwise comparison of the two images. -/
theorem sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_openSubspaceEquiv
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (sliceRingSheaf U)}
    (φ : F ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)) (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ) :
    sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := openSubspaceSheaf U)
        ((openSubspaceEquiv U).functor.map φ)) V =
      sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := X.sheaf.over U) φ)
        (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)) :=
  sectionIdeal_idealOfHom_openSubspace U φ ((openSubspaceEquiv U).functor.map φ)
    (fun _ _ => Iff.rfl) V

/-! ### The descent along the identified quotient, at the open-subspace spelling -/

variable (I : Stacks.Sites.IdealSubsheaf.{u, u, u} (X.sheaf.over U))
  (I' : Stacks.Sites.IdealSubsheaf.{u, u, u} (openSubspaceSheaf U))
  (hI' : ∀ V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ, sectionIdeal I' V =
    sectionIdeal I (op ((openSubspaceSiteFunctor U).obj V.unop)))

include hI' in
/-- **The comparison of the two quotients, with its source and target written as the targets of
the two quotient maps.** The ascription is what lets instance search see the comparison as a
morphism between the sheaves of rings the two descents fix, rather than between the two spellings
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceRingQuotientIso` writes them with. -/
abbrev openSubspaceQuotientCompare :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (quotientRingSheaf.{u, u, u} I') ⟶
      openSubspaceRingSheaf U
        (R' := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (quotientRingSheaf.{u, u, u} I)) :=
  (openSubspaceRingQuotientIso U I I' hI').hom

include hI' in
/-- **The comparison of the two quotients is locally surjective**, being an isomorphism. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_openSubspaceQuotientCompare :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U)
      (openSubspaceQuotientCompare U I I' hI').hom :=
  Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_iso (openSubspaceRingQuotientIso U I I' hI').hom

/-- **The quotient of the structure sheaf of `X.restrict U` and the open-subspace reading of the
slice quotient, as two locally surjective quotient maps out of one sheaf of rings identified by a
comparison.** This is the triple `(α₁, α₂, θ)` that
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.descendRingIsoHom` consumes, read off
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.quotientRingHom_comp_openSubspaceRingQuotientIso_hom`. -/
theorem quotientRingHom_comp_openSubspaceRingQuotientIso_hom' :
    quotientRingHom I' ≫ openSubspaceQuotientCompare U I I' hI' =
      openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom I) :=
  quotientRingHom_comp_openSubspaceRingQuotientIso_hom U I I' hI'

include hI' in
/-- **One annihilation hypothesis serves for both descents.** The comparison being an
isomorphism, a section of the structure sheaf of `X.restrict U` killed by the quotient formed
there is killed by the open-subspace reading of the slice quotient, and conversely. -/
theorem smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (openSubspaceRing U))
    (hA : ∀ (n : ℤ) (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ)
      (b : (openSubspaceRing U).obj.obj V),
      b ∈ RingHom.ker ((quotientRingHom I').hom.app V).hom →
        ∀ m : (A.piece n).val.obj V, b • m = 0)
    (n : ℤ) (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ) (b : (openSubspaceRing U).obj.obj V)
    (hb : b ∈ RingHom.ker
      ((openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom I)).hom.app V).hom)
    (m : (A.piece n).val.obj V) : b • m = 0 :=
  hA n V b (ChangeOfRings.ker_eq_ker_of_ringIso (quotientRingHom I')
    (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom I))
    (openSubspaceQuotientCompare U I I' hI')
    (quotientRingHom_comp_openSubspaceRingQuotientIso_hom' U I I' hI')
    (openSubspaceRingQuotientIso U I I' hI') rfl V ▸ hb) m

/-- **The universal property of an exterior algebra crosses the identification of the two
quotients of the structure sheaf over `U`.** Let `A` be a sheaf of graded algebras on
`X.restrict U` annihilated by the kernel of the quotient formed there. If its descent along that
quotient is the exterior algebra of the restriction of scalars of `M` on the generator read
through the transport, then its descent along the open-subspace reading of the slice quotient is
the exterior algebra of `M` on the generator itself.

This is `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.isExteriorAlgebra_descend_of_ringIso` instantiated at the
open-subspace spelling — the step the gluing of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] needs and the one whose
instantiation the two spellings of the slice structure sheaf blocked. The second annihilation
hypothesis is not asked for: the comparison is an isomorphism, so the two quotient maps have the
same kernel. -/
theorem isExteriorAlgebra_descend_openSubspaceRingQuotient
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (openSubspaceRing U))
    (hA : ∀ (n : ℤ) (V : (Opens ↥U)ᵒᵖ)
      (b : (openSubspaceRing U).obj.obj V),
      b ∈ RingHom.ker ((quotientRingHom I').hom.app V).hom →
        ∀ m : (A.piece n).val.obj V, b • m = 0)
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      (openSubspaceRingSheaf U (R' := toRingCat ((Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U)
        (quotientRingSheaf.{u, u, u} I)))}
    {ι : M ⟶ (descend (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom I)) A
      (smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward U I I' hI' A hA)).piece 1}
    (h : IsExteriorAlgebra (descend (quotientRingHom I') A hA)
      (genScalarRestrict (openSubspaceQuotientCompare U I I' hI') ι ≫
        (descendRingIsoHom (quotientRingHom I')
          (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom I))
          (openSubspaceQuotientCompare U I I' hI')
          (quotientRingHom_comp_openSubspaceRingQuotientIso_hom' U I I' hI') A hA
          (smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward U I I' hI' A hA)).app 1)) :
    IsExteriorAlgebra (descend (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom I)) A
      (smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward U I I' hI' A hA)) ι :=
  isExteriorAlgebra_descend_of_ringIso (quotientRingHom I')
    (openSubspaceQuotientHom U (quotientRingHom I))
    (openSubspaceQuotientCompare U I I' hI')
    (quotientRingHom_comp_openSubspaceRingQuotientIso_hom' U I I' hI') A hA
    (smul_eq_zero_of_mem_ker_openSubspaceRingPushforward U I I' hI' A hA) h

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
